sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch08-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The form of a growing organism regulates the form and number of the cells that compose it: the cell network is the result, not the cause, of the overall configuration, which is caused by whatever processes make growth faster in one direction than another.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cell division pattern is the result, not the cause, of the form of the growing mass";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter VIII, “The Forms of Tissues, or Cell-Aggregates (continued)”; topic “Growth form determines cell division”. Scope: growing multicellular plant and animal structures"
}
